    "prompt": "[GENERATION GOAL]\nA 27-second 16:9 photoreal cinematic short of a crying bearded survivor aims a pistol at his infected lover in a ruined kitchen. She snarls and screams. He cannot shoot, opens his arms, she screams again and lunges and strikes his face — hard smash-cut into golden-hour memories of the same couple in a wheat field. No gunshot. No extra plot.\n[GLOBAL STYLE]\n16:9 widescreen live-action cinema, 24fps, fine 35mm grain, shallow depth of field, natural skin, real tears.\nPRESENT (0–11s): cold desaturated dusty teal-grey, low-key, crushed blacks, overcast window light, slight handheld.\nMEMORY (11–27s): warm golden-hour amber and peach, volumetric sun, backlit wheat, gentle flare, smoother camera.\nReal-time only. No slow motion. No titles.\n[CHARACTERS]\nPRESENT MAN: <<<image_1>>> late 40s, dark messy hair, dark black and white beard and mustache, thin dried blood streak on the left forehead, tears on both cheeks. Dirty olive-green hooded anorak / short poncho with high collar, black chest harness, strap across the torso, small pouch on the left chest. The garment spreads like a cape when both arms open.\nINFECTED WOMAN: <<<image_2>>> mid-30s, same woman as the memory half. Dirty tangled blonde hair stuck to her face, grime in the skin, milky-white cloudy eyes, lips pulled back from teeth, small hoop earring, torn dirty grey-brown rag shirt, dark worn trousers. She SNARLS and SCREAMS — mouth wide, teeth showing, a raw guttural scream, not a quiet growl, not a movie-monster roar. She is sick and feral, still recognizably the healthy woman, not a generic rotting zombie, not a different actress.\nMEMORY MAN: <<<image_1>>> same face, well groomed beard  in all scenes, no blood, no tears. Off-white linen button shirt.\nMEMORY WOMAN <<<image_3>>>: same woman healthy — long wavy blonde hair, white teeth, eyes crinkled from laughing. Thin gold necklace. Flowing white/cream linen dress.\n[LOCATIONS]\nKITCHEN: abandoned farmhouse. Peeling plaster, wooden cabinets, shelves with a silver pot and a red tin, white plastic jug, yellow mop by a 4-pane window onto pale trees, dark wooden door on camera-left, dusty air.\nFIELD: tall golden wheat on rolling hills, distant mountains, low sun.\n[SHOT-ACCURATE TIMELINE — 16:9]\n0.0–2.0s\nSHOT A. Extreme close-up of the PRESENT MAN <<<image_1>>>, framed for 16:9 (head and shoulders, slight left bias). Tears, blood on the left forehead. A black compact pistol fills the right foreground, out of focus, aimed at camera. Tiny handheld drift. He does not fire.\n<quiet tense drone, shaky breath>\nDistant, muffled wet snarl from off-screen.\n2.0–3.5s\nSHOT B. Hard cut. Over-the-shoulder from behind his left shoulder, 16:9. He is a dark blur left. Pistol a small dark shape center. INFECTED WOMAN <<<image_2>>> full-body in the kitchen, slack arms, staring. Slight movement. Cabinets, red tin, white jug, yellow mop behind her.\n<wet snarl, floor creak>\n3.5–4.5s\nSHOT C. Medium, eye-level, man centered in 16:9. Two-handed pistol aimed at camera. Olive anorak and harness visible. Window right, doorway left, yellow mop. He cries and holds aim.\n4.5–6.2s\nSHOT D. Extreme close-up of the INFECTED WOMAN <<<image_2>>>, 16:9. Milky-white eyes, dirt in the pores, teeth bared. She SNARLS hard into camera — jaw wide, spit, throat working, hair stuck to her face, hoop earring visible.\n<wet snarl, breath hitch>\n6.2–7.5s\nSHOT E. Extreme close-up of the PRESENT MAN <<<image_1>>>. Tears running but does not shoot. Hold.\n7.5–8.5s\nSHOT F. Same medium as Shot C. Still aiming two-handed. Then he starts lowering the pistol. She keeps a low continuous snarl under the picture.\n8.5–10.2s\nSHOT G. Same camera. He drops the gun to his right side and slowly opens both arms wide, palms forward. Poncho-anorak spreads, harness and left-chest pouch readable. Tears on his face. Eyes start to close.\nUnderneath: her snarl rising again into scream.\n10.2–11.0s\nSHOT H. Side-on medium, 16:9. Man in profile left. Bright blown-out window behind them. INFECTED WOMAN <<<image_2>>> lunges as a dark silhouette, SCREAMING, and her hand strikes / grabs his face. One violent second. No gore\n<full-throat scream on the lunge, body impact, score slams in>\n11.0s\n\nHARD SMASH CUT. No dissolve. Cold grey flips to warm gold in one frame. Her scream cuts off with the picture.\n11.0–13.0s\nSHOT I. Low-angle medium in tall backlit wheat, 16:9. MEMORY MAN <<<image_1>>>  in a light shirt holds MEMORY WOMAN against him. Wheat blowing, sun flaring behind the hill.\n13.0–16.0s\nSHOT J. Close-up of MEMORY WOMAN <<<image_3>>> leaning over him, laughing, eyes almost shut, freckles in the sun. His hand cups her cheek and jaw. Bright sky behind her. No dialogue.\n16.0–18.0s\nSHOT K. Close-up of MEMORY MAN <<<image_1>>>  on his back in grass and tiny yellow flowers. Light stubble, dappled sun, soft smile, looking up at her. Gold ring on her hand.\n18.0–21.0s\nSHOT L. Wide from behind, 16:9. They walk away hand-in-hand through backlit wheat toward the sun. Gentle follow, wheat in the foreground.\n21.0–23.0s\nSHOT M. Medium from behind. They sit in the grass, his arm around her, orange sun on the horizon. He kisses the side of her head.\n23.0–27.0s\nSHOT N. Wide landscape, 16:9. Couple small in the lower third of the hill, pink-orange sunset, layered mountains, tall grass foreground. Hold.\n(warm sparse piano and low strings from 10s, sad, never loud)\n<wheat wind, cloth rustle, her laugh only as breath — no speech in the memory half>\n[AUDIO — REQUIRED]\nInfected woman: wet SNARL + raw SCREAM. must be loud and on-camera in Shot D, must peak again on the Shot H lunge.\nNo spoken words. No gunshot. No male scream.\nPresent bed: tense low drone, breath, wood creak.\nAt"
