    "prompt": "<<<image_1>>> cake identity only. Preserve the birthday cake's overall shape, proportions, size, decoration style, colors, frosting design, candle arrangement and distinctive visual details. Do not transfer the reference background, pose, camera angle or lighting. Keep the same recognizable cake design throughout the video.\n<<<image_2>>> vehicle identity only. Preserve the vehicle's recognizable body shape, proportions, paimnt color, wheel design, lighting elements and distinctive exterior features. Do not transfer the reference background, pose, camera angle or lighting. Keep the same recognizable vehicle design throughout the entire video with no morphing.\n\n<<<image_3>>> = subject identity only. Preserve the recognizable face, facial structure, eyes, skin tone, hair and apparent age of the subject shown in <<<image_3>>>. Do not transfer the reference background, pose, camera angle or lighting. Keep the same recognizable subject throughout the video from every visible angle. The prompt must work equally well for any subject provided in <<<image_3>>>, regardless of gender.\n\nSCENE\n\nFirst-person POV shot outdoors in open space, filmed as one continuous take.\n\nThe unseen POV person is standing still and holding the birthday cake from <<<image_1>>> close to the camera in the foreground. The cake is supported naturally in the POV hands and remains visible for most of the shot. The cake has many small lit candles, all clearly burning.\n\nFrom the distance, the vehicle from <<<image_2>>> rushes toward the camera at high speed and enters in a dramatic controlled drift with visible sideways motion and tire slip.\n\nThe subject from <<<image_3>>> is leaning halfway out of the driver-side front window of the moving vehicle, upper body outside the window, clearly visible during the drift.\n\nACTION\n\n0.0–1.5s:\nThe shot begins in first-person POV. The birthday cake from <<<image_1>>> many lit candles fills the lower foreground. The unseen POV holder keeps the cake steady in front of the camera. In the distance, the vehicle from <<<image_2>>> rapidly approaches.\n1.5–5.5s:\nAs soon as the vehicle begins its fast drift approach, the motion enters cinematic slow motion. The vehicle does not brake or pause before the close pass. It continues moving fast in one smooth, controlled drifting approach toward the POV, sliding sideways in a dramatic arc. The subject from <<<image_3>>> is already leaning halfway out of the driver-side window, facing toward the cake and camera.\n\n5.5–6.5s:\nDuring the closest point of the drifting slow-motion pass, the subject from <<<image_3>>> leans further outward from the window and blows toward the cake from <<<image_1>>>. The blow must clearly extinguish the candles. The candle flames react naturally, flicker, and go out as a direct result of the subject's blowing action.\n\n6.5–8.0s:\nImmediately at the strongest visual peak — when the drifting vehicle is closest, the subject is extended from the window, and the candles have just been extinguished — transition into a dramatic high-contrast black-and-white freeze frame. Hold this black-and-white frozen final frame for approximately 2 seconds. Do not continue with the vehicle driving away.\n\nCAMERA\n\nFirst-person POV only.\n\nThe entire video is filmed as if seen through the eyes of the unseen cake-holder.\n\nThe camera remains in one position with only subtle natural body movement from the POV holder.\n\nNo cuts, no angle changes, no third-person shots, no drone view.\n\nThe cake from <<<image_1>>> Freeze-frame lock: the final 2 seconds must be a dramatic black-and-white still frame at the peak moment.\n\nAUDIO\n\nMinimal synchronized physical Foley only.\n\nDistant fast-approaching tire and engine sound at first, growing louder as the vehicle nears.\n\nA controlled drifting tire sound during the slide.\n\nOne clear human blowing breath from the subject exactly when the subject blows toward the candles.\n\nSubtle candle extinguish behavior.\n\nAt the freeze-frame moment, let the final audio hit decay naturally or stop cleanly.\n\nNo music. No dialogue.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\n\nSingle continuous take. No cuts.\n\nFirst-person POV only.\n\nThe cake held in the foreground must match <<<image_1>>> in overall appearance and candle arrangement.\n\nThe vehicle from <<<image_2>>> must approach at high speed and perform a close controlled drift pass near the POV.\n\nThe movement must feel stylish, fast and controlled, not like the car is stopping in front of the POV holder.\n\nDo not show the vehicle braking, pausing or awkwardly slowing down before the closest pass.\n\nSlow motion must begin during the fast drifting approach itself, while the vehicle is still actively closing distance toward the POV.\n\nDo not delay the slow motion until after the vehicle has nearly stopped or after the subject starts leaning toward the cake.\n\nThe subject from <<<image_3>>> must be leaning halfway out of the driver-side front window, clearly visible while the vehicle is drifting.\n\nThe subject must blow out the candles during the closest pass of the drifting vehicle.\n\nThe candles must go out only as a direct result of the subject's blowing action.\n\nDo not continue into an awkward or unnatural drive-away ending.\n\nInstead, end the video at the climax with a dramatic black-and-white freeze frame held for about 2 seconds.\n\nDo not add extra people.\n\nDo not change the cake design.\n\nDo not change the vehicle design.\n\nDo not change the subject identity.\n\nNo champagne, no champagne bottle, no champagne spray, and no celebratory liquid effects.\n\nNo text, captions, subtitles, logos or graphic overlays. <<<image_1>>>"
